# Build output. `pocctl`, `watch` and `poc` are built by `scripts/verify.ps1`
# and by `pocctl demo`; they are not sources and are not committed.
/bin/
/.demo-data/
/.poc-data/

# A run's data root. It holds the rolling recording, the evidence store and the
# SQLite database, and it is the operator's to choose where it goes. The default
# the demo uses is inside the module, and a run's output is never a source.
/.poc-final/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
/poc.db*

# The model. Not in git: it is 250 MB, it is downloaded, and a model with no
# recorded provenance is a model nobody checked. `pocctl fetch-model` puts it
# here and the README says where it came from.
/models/

# Downloaded video, in ANY directory under testdata/.
#
# The committed clips are the ones named in testdata/labels.json with their
# provenance, licence and retrieval date. Footage pulled off somebody else's site
# is NOT one of them: a downloaded clip is not a source, and committing one would
# republish material the camera operator never agreed to give away.
#
# This pattern is deliberately broad. It was `youtube/` only, and a second
# download into `youtube2/` was about to be committed — which is exactly the
# accident this rule exists to prevent.
testdata/youtube*/
testdata/live*/
*.mp4.part
*.replaced
*.pick.png
*.pick.jpg

# A run's measured output, same category as /.demo-data/ above. `.live-data/` and
# `.real-data/` hold a full run's SQLite store and its report; they are produced
# by `pocctl demo`, they are reproducible by re-running it, and committing one
# means committing a measurement of footage this repository may not redistribute.
# The plan reads them as evidence while a run is on disk, not as sources.
/.live-data/
/.real-data/

# A stray log written by a recording or a demo run from the repository root.
# Nothing names it, nothing reads it, and it is 130 KB of somebody else's frames.
/record*.log

# The staged report and one-pager are generated artefacts. They are produced by
# `pocctl report` and by `scripts/make-one-pager.sh` from a run's own store, so
# committing one means committing a measurement that nobody can reproduce from
# the tree.
/testdata/.demo-report.md
/docs/one-pager.md

# A raw provider response, from `pocctl vlm-probe`.
#
# It is the provider's own words about a customer's clip, written to a file on this
# machine by a command an operator ran by hand. It is evidence for the person who ran
# the probe and for nobody else until they have read it and chosen to share it. The
# directory keeps a `.gitkeep` so the path the README names exists.
contracts/hafnia/raw/*
!contracts/hafnia/raw/.gitkeep

# __pycache__ from the sidecar's tests.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# QA lab fixtures. Regenerated by: bash qa/make-fixtures.sh qa/fixtures
qa/fixtures/*.mp4
qa/fixtures/*.png
qa/fixtures/*.rgb
qa/fixtures/*.gray

